{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/359927-sin-eaters-and-player-death","id":359927,"title":"Sin-Eaters and Player Death","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-04T23:47:21-08:00","id":359927,"title":"Sin-Eaters and Player Death","content":"Hallo. I recently skimmed over a thread in the Werewolf forums, in which a dude was very torn on wether or not to kill his players, because they were being suicidal, and it got me thinking.<br /> How do you treat player death in a game in which all players can come back from death like 4 times before shit gets real?<br /> Personally - althought no player death has yet sprung up in my game - I would it treat much more freely than normally. If a player does something immensely stupid, they die. Mercilessly and brutally. Even if &quot;Something stupid&quot; is just walking into the slums at night, to shadow that shady group of men in suits who all mumble in a long dead-tongue. If they failed that, and the subsequent roll to run the fuck away, I'de probably feel inclined to have them killed.<br /> <br /> But how do you treat it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T02:42:28-08:00","id":360041,"title":"","content":"I don't use character death as a stick. It can happen, though it is unlikely unless it seems a dramatic point for such to happen.<br /> <br /> As such, I don't run Geist any different than Changeling or Demon. Character Death is a bad 